d": 44054082, "text": "Writers use similes to help us understand what they are describing more clearly, for instance: ‘as cute as a kitten’. In this simile, ‘cute’ is made clearer by being compared to a kitten – we all know how cute they are! The simile wouldn’t work as well if it said ‘as cute as a horse’ because although horses are nice, they aren’t cute in the same way as kittens are.", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 1, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{'headers':['Col1'],'rows':[{'col1':'row1'},{'col1':'row2'}, {'col1':'row3'}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 44053973, "dimensions": null, "editAsHtml": false, "properties": {"height": "", "fontArray": [[]], "inputArray": [[]], "widthArray": [[""]]}, "deletedById": null, "downloadUrl": null, "editorState": null, "carouselData": null, "downloadName": null, "accordionData": null, "includeSeconds": null, "selectedModalId": 0, "textCarouselData": "{ \"text\": [] }", "checkListTextData": null, "imageCarouselData": null, "checklistImageData": null, "clickableAlphabetData": null}, {"id": 44054343, "text": "<h2>Challenge:</h2>\nSometimes writers use unexpected comparisons in similes to make a point. For instance, ‘as clear as mud’ means ‘not clear at all’, since mud is definitely not see-through. \n<br></br>\nCan you finish these similes in the same way?\n", "modal": {"steps": [null], "details": null}, "order": 7, "btnType": null, "linkUrl": null, "audioUrl": null, "fileName": null, "fontSize": null, "fontType": "SassoonInfantRg-Regular", "imageUrl": null, "linkName": null, "stepType": "TEXT_AND_IMAGE", "tabsData": null, "deletedAt": null, "tableData": "{'headers':['Col1'],'rows':[{'col1':'row1'},{'col1':'row2'}, {'col1':'row3'}]}", "timerData": null, "activityId": 44053973, "dimensions":